+
+Check filesystem free space and packet bytes before every compile/test/export
+stage, poll compilation growth, and stop before another stage if the approved
+floor/cap cannot accommodate its remaining reservation. A 300 MiB soft-abort
+threshold leaves 20 MiB under the cap for observation/termination latency; this
+is monitoring, not a filesystem guarantee. Any unexpected dependency build is
+a stop, not a reason to switch targets silently. Preserve failures. A further
+candidate binary after a failed completed build is not silently squeezed into
